 "deck_playtime_at_review": 136, "last_played": 1660268417, "avatar": "511fc7a4a2ddbd1e9d1355f57cd7a068582eaf19"}, "language": "english", "review": "This is one of those games where you want  to start it with the cliched \"if only there was a neutral button\"...\n\nIf you are at least somewhat aware of the 40k universe it is cool to see it in action game form. However the game itself just isn't that good. Combat, which should be the bread and butter of this game -- just doesn't feel that interesting. The game alternates between melee and ranged combat at your discretion, but neither feel particularly fun or interesting. As the difficulty increases, there is a bit more strategy involved with what weapon to use and whether to use melee or ranged, but the combat is still pretty bland. But the setting is nice; it's 40k but it's the badass side of 40k rather than the darker side. The main character is quite likable, being polite to people below his rank and being generally badass.", "timestamp_created": 1659148418, "timestamp_updated": 1659148418, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": true, "app_release_date": "1315281600", "reactions": []}]}